# ============================================================================
# SentenceTTS Reader — what git must NOT track
# Rule of thumb: anything regenerable from a build script is ignored; anything
# that CANNOT be regenerated (the Chrome signing key!) is ignored too, but for
# the opposite reason — it must never leave this machine except into a backup.
# ============================================================================

# ---- The private RSA key that fixes the Chrome extension ID ----------------
# NEVER commit this. It is what pins the extension ID
#   b6ecf49b455c8c297c695d998f40d28a
# (first 32 hex chars of SHA-256 over the SPKI DER) and therefore the Piper
# native-messaging `allowed_origins`. Losing it means a new extension ID and
# orphaned installs. `build-source/build-chrome.js` exits 1 when it is missing
# rather than silently minting a different ID, so a clone without the key still
# builds — it just cannot reproduce the published ID.
#
# Verify a restored backup with:
#   openssl pkey -in build-source/chrome-key.pem -pubout -outform DER | sha256sum
#   -> must start with  b6ecf49b455c8c297c695d998f40d28a
build-source/chrome-key.pem
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx

# ---- Build output: fully regenerated, never a source of truth -------------
# chrome-build/ is assembled from the repo root by build-chrome.js, including
# manifest.json (key baked in), piper-host-manifest.json and
# install-piper-host.sh (both generated inside that script).
chrome-build/

# Submission bundles. Chrome: produced by build-chrome.js.
# Firefox: the `zip -r` line in build-source/BUILD.md.
/*.zip

# ---- Vendored deps stay COMMITTED (vendor/ is not listed here on purpose) --
# vendor/kokoro/ is checked in deliberately: kokoro-js + the ONNX Runtime wasm
# ship inside the extension and must be byte-identical to what was reviewed by
# AMO. Largest file is 21 MB (ort-wasm-…jsep.wasm), comfortably under GitHub's
# 100 MB per-file cap, so no Git LFS is required.

# ---- Python (piper-host native messaging host) ----------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# ---- Node -----------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# ---- Test scratch ---------------------------------------------------------
# The e2e scripts currently resolve playwright-core out of /tmp/e2e and want
# PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH=/tmp/pw-browsers (see AGENT.md open item 6). If that
# bootstrap ever moves in-tree, keep the artifacts out of git anyway.
test-results/
playwright-report/
/tmp-e2e/

# ---- Local agent / editor / OS cruft --------------------------------------
.claude/settings.local.json
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
*.log
